$$SYNTAX-LEVEL 2
*(mgdb-archive
<main class="mgdb-page mgdb-archive-page" id="archive-main">
  <nav class="mgdb-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/data_center/">Data hubs</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><span aria-current="page">Archived data hubs</span>
  </nav>

  <section class="mgdb-hero archive-hero" aria-labelledby="archive-title">
    <div class="mgdb-hero-emblem">
      <svg class="archive-hero-mark" viewBox="0 0 132 116" role="img" aria-label="Five archival collection drawers">
        <rect x="14" y="10" width="104" height="96" rx="10" fill="#f4edd0" stroke="#a96919" stroke-width="4" />
        <g>
          <rect x="24" y="20" width="84" height="14" rx="4" fill="#501719" /><rect x="24" y="38" width="84" height="14" rx="4" fill="#2f5e2a" /><rect x="24" y="56" width="84" height="14" rx="4" fill="#a96919" /><rect x="24" y="74" width="84" height="14" rx="4" fill="#501719" /><rect x="24" y="92" width="84" height="6" rx="3" fill="#2f5e2a" />
        </g>
        <g fill="#f4edd0"><rect x="59" y="24" width="14" height="5" rx="2" /><rect x="59" y="42" width="14" height="5" rx="2" /><rect x="59" y="60" width="14" height="5" rx="2" /><rect x="59" y="78" width="14" height="5" rx="2" /></g>
      </svg>
      <strong>MaizeGDB<br />Archives</strong>
      <span>Research history preserved</span>
    </div>
    <div class="mgdb-hero-body">
      <span class="mgdb-eyebrow">Historical MaizeGDB collections</span>
      <h1 id="archive-title">Preserving maize research history.</h1>
      <p class="mgdb-hero-tagline">Explore legacy data hubs without losing the path to current maize resources.</p>
      <p class="mgdb-hero-description">MaizeGDB does not delete scientific data. These collections preserve records, evidence, and interfaces that remain important for reproducing earlier research, even though they are no longer actively updated.</p>
      <div class="mgdb-hero-actions">
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="#archived-collections">Browse archived collections</a>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="/data_center/">Explore current data hubs</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mgdb-message mgdb-message-info archive-guidance" role="status">
    <div><strong>Historical context matters.</strong> Use these collections when following older publications, clone names, probes, marker systems, cytological maps, or legacy accessions. For new analyses, begin with the current resources linked from each card.</div>
  </div>

  <section aria-labelledby="archive-summary-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><span class="mgdb-eyebrow">Archive at a glance</span><h2 id="archive-summary-title">Five collections, connected to today</h2></div>
      <p>Every archive remains searchable or browsable and retains links into the wider MaizeGDB knowledge graph.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mgdb-metric-grid">
      <article class="mgdb-metric"><span class="mgdb-metric-icon" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div><strong class="mgdb-metric-value">5</strong><h3>Preserved data hubs</h3><p>Physical maps, chromosomes, transcripts, probes, and markers.</p></div></article>
      <article class="mgdb-metric mgdb-tone-green"><span class="mgdb-metric-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#8981;</span><div><strong class="mgdb-metric-value mgdb-metric-value-compact">Searchable</strong><h3>Record access</h3><p>Legacy names, identifiers, motifs, and scientific relationships remain available.</p></div></article>
      <article class="mgdb-metric mgdb-tone-red"><span class="mgdb-metric-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span><div><strong class="mgdb-metric-value mgdb-metric-value-compact">Connected</strong><h3>Modern pathways</h3><p>Each collection points to a current genome, gene, marker, or expression resource.</p></div></article>
      <article class="mgdb-metric mgdb-tone-burgundy"><span class="mgdb-metric-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#9633;</span><div><strong class="mgdb-metric-value mgdb-metric-value-compact">Archived</strong><h3>Update status</h3><p>Preserved for historical use; not actively curated or expanded.</p></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="archived-collections" aria-labelledby="archived-collections-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><span class="mgdb-eyebrow">Choose a collection</span><h2 id="archived-collections-title">Archived data hubs</h2></div>
      <p>Each card explains what the archive preserves and where to begin for contemporary research.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="archive-collection-grid">
      <article class="archive-collection-card archive-bac">
        <div class="archive-card-top"><span class="mgdb-pill mgdb-pill-info">Physical mapping</span><span class="archive-card-code" aria-hidden="true">BAC</span></div>
        <h3>BAC clone archive</h3>
        <p>Search bacterial artificial chromosome clone names, synonyms, accessions, sequences, and physical-map relationships from historical B73 assemblies.</p>
        <div class="archive-card-actions"><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="/data_center/bac">Open BAC archive</a><a href="/genome/assembly/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0">Current B73 reference <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></div>
      </article>

      <article class="archive-collection-card archive-cytogenetic">
        <div class="archive-card-top"><span class="mgdb-pill mgdb-pill-ok">Chromosome biology</span><span class="archive-card-code" aria-hidden="true">CYTO</span></div>
        <h3>Cytogenetics resources</h3>
        <p>Explore cytological maps, chromosome landmarks, karyotype and FISH imagery, structural-variant stocks, and foundational cytogenetics references.</p>
        <div class="archive-card-actions"><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="/data_center/cytogenetic">Open Cytogenetics</a><a href="/genome">Current genome resources <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></div>
      </article>

      <article class="archive-collection-card archive-est">
        <div class="archive-card-top"><span class="mgdb-pill mgdb-pill-warn">Transcript evidence</span><span class="archive-card-code" aria-hidden="true">EST</span></div>
        <h3>Expressed sequence tags</h3>
        <p>Find EST names, sequence identifiers, GenBank accessions, legacy library patterns, annotations, detected loci, and mapped transcript evidence.</p>
        <div class="archive-card-actions"><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="/data_center/est">Open EST collection</a><a href="/expression">Current expression data <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></div>
      </article>

      <article class="archive-collection-card archive-overgo">
        <div class="archive-card-top"><span class="mgdb-pill">Mapping probes</span><span class="archive-card-code" aria-hidden="true">OV</span></div>
        <h3>Overgo probe archive</h3>
        <p>Search Overgo probe names and short sequences used to connect clones, loci, physical maps, and early maize genome projects.</p>
        <div class="archive-card-actions"><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="/data_center/overgo">Open Overgo archive</a><a href="/data_center/marker">Current marker search <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></div>
      </article>

      <article class="archive-collection-card archive-ssr">
        <div class="archive-card-top"><span class="mgdb-pill mgdb-pill-info">Microsatellite markers</span><span class="archive-card-code" aria-hidden="true">SSR</span></div>
        <h3>SSR marker archive</h3>
        <p>Search simple sequence repeat names, synonyms, motifs, primers, gel patterns, mapped-marker files, and historical mapping protocols.</p>
        <div class="archive-card-actions"><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="/data_center/ssr">Open SSR archive</a><a href="/data_center/marker">Current marker search <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mgdb-prose-layout archive-use-layout" aria-labelledby="archive-use-title">
    <div class="mgdb-prose">
      <span class="mgdb-eyebrow">Working with historical data</span>
      <h2 id="archive-use-title" class="mgdb-leaf-heading">Use the archive with its original context</h2>
      <p>Legacy identifiers and coordinates may refer to older assemblies, map versions, nomenclature, or laboratory methods. Record the collection name, identifiers, map or assembly version, and access date when using archived material.</p>
      <p>Follow linked loci, genes, sequences, references, and maps to understand how a historical record relates to current MaizeGDB data.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="mgdb-aside-card archive-help-card">
      <span class="mgdb-eyebrow">Need help locating a record?</span>
      <h3>Start with the archive, then follow its links.</h3>
      <p>If an older identifier does not resolve, contact MaizeGDB with the identifier, publication, and collection where it appeared.</p>
      <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="/contact">Contact MaizeGDB</a>
    </aside>
  </section>
</main>
)
